    {
      "id": "u07-l3",
      "title": "Likes",
      "goal": "Say what you love, like and hate, with the right article.",
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": "u07-l3-n1",
          "title": "Likes take an article",
          "body": "With **aimer**, **adorer** and **détester**, put an article before the thing you like or hate: **le** (m), **la** (f), **l'** (vowel), **les** (plural). It means *in general*, so **j'aime le café** means *I like coffee* as a drink. Keep the article, even though English drops it.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "J'aime la musique.",
              "en": "I like music."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Je déteste le sport.",
              "en": "I hate sport."
            },
            {
              "fr": "J'adore les films.",
              "en": "I love films."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u07-l3-n2",
          "title": "Love, like, hate",
          "body": "**adorer** is the strongest: *to love*. **aimer** is *to like*. **détester** is *to hate*. Add **bien** after **aimer** to soften it: *j'aime bien* (I quite like). To say you don't, wrap **ne … pas** around the verb: *je n'aime pas* (I don't like).",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "J'adore les films.",
              "en": "I love films."
            },
            {
              "fr": "J'aime bien le sport.",
              "en": "I quite like sport."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Je n'aime pas le café.",
              "en": "I don't like coffee."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
